[Jaune Quick-to-See Smith: Summer Exhibition]

 Jaune Quick-to-See Smith (1940–2025) was one of the most important and groundbreaking Native American artists of the past century. This exhibition follows The Art of Memories Told, a show of Smith’s works on paper held by LewAllen in early spring of this year. That show had been planned before it was known that the artist was dying.&#x20;

…

In this spirit, it is no surprise that Smith wished her work to be seen alongside that of so many Native American artists, during a time and in a community that meant so much to her. This second exhibition features a major mixed-media painting by Smith: Arlee Ledger Pony (2015), 40 x 60 inches, mixed media on canvas. In this important painting, imbued with biographical significance, Smith utilizes the visual language of Native American ledger art, pulling it into the present and creating contemporary cultural continuity.&#x20;

